      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockland%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town claims it was founded in 1879, eleven years before Idaho became a state.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockland%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Trappers first traversed the Rockland Valley, but permanent settlers arrived in 1878 to farm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockland%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Guadalupe Valdez was the valley’s first irrigated farmer, digging a ditch from East Fork Creek to water his 30 acres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
